
[TestRequireAbortSignalInWhile/invalid-0 - 1]
Diagnostic 1: requireAbortSignalInWhile (1:28 - 1:61)
Message: A `while` condition must test an abort signal.
Help: Add `!<signal>.aborted &&` to the condition so the loop ends when the signal aborts, and keep the real stop conditions alongside it.
   1 | declare let taken: number; while (taken < 10) { taken += 1; }
     |                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
